{#
    Submit button with a real progress bar, shared by every panel that runs a query.

    The backend knows how far along it is — exactly for the filtered graph (bins done /
    bins total), approximately for a single-shot nfdump (bytes read / bytes to read) — so
    the button shows per-mille progress and an ETA instead of an indeterminate spinner.

    Falls back to the spinner automatically: when `permille` is 0 and no status text has
    arrived, there is nothing meaningful to draw yet.

    Params:
      label      — idle button text
      action     — action URL to POST on click
      running    — server-owned bool signal, true while the query runs
      permille   — server-owned int signal, 0..1000
      status     — server-owned string signal, e.g. "Scanning 42 / 288 intervals"
      eta        — server-owned string signal, e.g. "~1m 30s"
      exact      — server-owned bool signal; false renders the figure as an estimate
      kindSignal — server-owned string signal naming the panel that owns the running query
      kind       — this panel's name; progress renders only when kindSignal matches it
      killAction — action URL for the Kill button
      id         — DOM id prefix, so several of these can coexist
      onClick    — optional extra JS to run before the POST
#}
{#
    Only this panel's own query drives its button. Panels sharing a screen share the query_*
    signals — the Flows tab carries both Process data and the traffic panel's Build graph — so
    without the kind check one query would light up the other's button.

    `disabled` still keys off the bare running flag: only one query runs at a time, so a
    click on another panel's button would be silently dropped.
#}
{% set here = '$' ~ running ~ " && $" ~ kindSignal ~ " === '" ~ kind ~ "'" %}
<div class="cluster" id="{{ id }}">
    <button type="button"
            data-variant="primary"
            id="{{ id }}Submit"
            data-attr:disabled="${{ running }}"
            data-on:click="{{ onClick|default('') }}@post('{{ action }}')">
        <span data-show="!({{ here }})">{{ label }}</span>
        <span class="spinner" data-show="{{ here }}" role="status" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span data-show="{{ here }}">Processing…</span>
    </button>

    <button type="button"
            class="kill"
            data-size="sm"
            style="display:none"
            data-show="{{ here }}"
            data-on:click="@post('{{ killAction }}')">Kill</button>

    {#
        Progress readout. The *bar* only exists while the query runs, but the status line
        outlives it — otherwise the closing "Done in 1.2s." / "Cancelled" message is set and
        hidden in the same breath, and the user never sees how the run ended.
    #}
    <div class="query-progress" style="display:none"
         data-show="({{ here }}) || (${{ status }} !== '' && ${{ kindSignal }} === '{{ kind }}')">
        <progress max="1000" style="display:none"
             data-show="{{ here }}"
             data-attr:data-indeterminate="!${{ exact }}"
             data-attr:value="${{ permille }}">
            {#
                Driven straight off the signal, so a syncSignals() patch moves it without the
                page being re-rendered. A native <progress> takes the permille as its value,
                which also gives assistive tech the reading for free.
            #}
        </progress>
        <div class="cluster cluster-between muted query-progress-line">
            <span data-text="${{ status }}"></span>
            <span data-show="{{ here }}">
                <span data-text="(${{ permille }} / 10).toFixed(1) + '%'"></span>
                <span data-show="!${{ exact }}" title="Estimated from bytes read">(est.)</span>
                <span data-show="${{ eta }} !== ''" data-text="' • ' + ${{ eta }}"></span>
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
